   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C before market introduction and at least annually thereafter, using a regulator-approved sampling protocol. The maximum failure rate is 5%. Manufacturers must submit per-model numerical results, sample sizes, test methods, and corrective actions to regulators, and must provide the numerical result for each model to customers who buy it. A model exceeding the limit must promptly submit an enforceable corrective-action plan and timetable to the regulator, complete corrective measures, and undergo a verified retest. Regulators may restrict sales where a manufacturer fails to implement its plan or where evidence indicates an imminent safety risk."
